{"name":"Splatter","hex":"#a9586c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"splatter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An uneven shape or mess created by something dispersing on impact.","A genre of gory horror."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To splash; to scatter; to land or strike in an uneven, distributed mess.","To cause (something) to splatter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splatter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blood squirt","blocks":[{"text":"Blood squirt is a projectile expulsion of blood when an artery is ruptured. Blood pressure causes the blood to bleed out at a rapid, intermittent rate in a spray or jet, coinciding with the pulse, rather than the slower, but steady flow of venous bleeding. Also known as arterial bleeding, arterial spurting, or arterial gushing, the amount of blood loss can be copious, occur very rapidly, and can lead to death by exsanguination."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Bengali_Chinnamasta.jpg/330px-Bengali_Chinnamasta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_squirt"},{"title":"Spectral splatter","blocks":[{"text":"In radio electronics or acoustics, spectral splatter refers to spurious emissions that result from an abrupt change in the transmitted signal, usually when transmission is started or stopped."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Splatter_from_an_illegal_CB_amplifier%2C_with_ionospheric_artifacts.png/330px-Splatter_from_an_illegal_CB_amplifier%2C_with_ionospheric_artifacts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spectral_splatter"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Splatter_Q9.jpg/500px-Splatter_Q9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Splatter_Q9.jpg/1280px-Splatter_Q9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Splatter_Q9.jpg/500px-Splatter_Q9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Frequency spectrum of a non-splattering PSK31 signal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASplatter_Q9.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Splatter_Q1.jpg/500px-Splatter_Q1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Splatter_Q1.jpg/1280px-Splatter_Q1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Splatter_Q1.jpg/500px-Splatter_Q1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Frequency spectrum of a splattering PSK31 signal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASplatter_Q1.jpg"}],"sounds":{"splatter":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4a/En-us-splatter.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/4a/En-us-splatter.ogg/En-us-splatter.ogg.mp3"}]}}}